  "marked": false,
  "answer": "<p>The correct answer is <b>Amazon EventBridge integrated with a Lambda function.</b> EventBridge is the successor to CloudWatch Events and offers a highly scalable and flexible solution for event-driven architectures. It allows you to ingest and distribute events not just from AWS services, but also from external SaaS platforms like PagerDuty, which is a unique capability required in this scenario. By connecting EventBridge to a Lambda function, you can process and respond to these events serverlessly.</p><p>Let's see why the other options are not suitable:</p><ul><li><i>CloudWatch Event plus a Lambda function</i>: CloudWatch Events is essentially the predecessor of EventBridge and does not natively support integration with third-party SaaS events at the scale and flexibility required. It is being subsumed by EventBridge features.</li><li><i>CloudTrail together with CloudWatch Event</i>: While CloudTrail logs account activity and CloudWatch Events can trigger actions based on AWS service changes, this combination does not provide the centralized, event-driven architecture needed for microservices or enable integration with SaaS event sources like PagerDuty.</li><li><i>EventBridge in combination with AWS Step Function</i>: While Step Functions orchestrate workflows, they are not primarily for ingesting and centrally routing events. EventBridge with Lambda is generally more appropriate for decoupled, event-driven microservice communication and SaaS event handling.</li></ul><p><b>Tip:</b> For redesigning applications for extensibility and loosely coupled microservices, always look for services that support central event buses and third-party event sources. That points directly to EventBridge.</p>",
  "query": "<p>As a DevOps engineer in a large enterprise, you're tasked with transforming a monolithic EC2-based application into a serverless, microservices architecture using AWS. The new solution should enable decoupled communication between components, centralize event handling, and support receiving events from third-party SaaS providers like PagerDuty. Which AWS service combination best fulfills these requirements?</p>",
